::GEO_U04_L03_Q01::
Question ID:<br>GEO_U04_L03_Q01<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.GEO.SIM.3<br><br>Question:<br>Two triangles have &angle;A &cong; &angle;D and &angle;B &cong; &angle;E. Which criterion justifies similarity? {
=A. AA similarity#Two congruent angle pairs are enough to prove triangle similarity.
~B. SSS similarity#SSS similarity requires all three side ratios.
~C. SAS similarity#SAS similarity requires two proportional side pairs and the included angle.
~D. HL congruence#HL proves congruence in right triangles, not similarity here. T
}

::GEO_U04_L03_Q02::
Question ID:<br>GEO_U04_L03_Q02<br><br>MLA Standard:<br><br><br>Question:<br> {
=B. #
}

